---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="About Manny Mayorga and the thinking behind Rough at Sea.">
  <section class="about-hero shell">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">ABOUT / MANNY MAYORGA</p>
      <h1>I like ideas that explain themselves.</h1>
    </div>
    <div class="about-intro">
      <p>I’m a reader and a note-keeper in Arizona interested in the seam between observation and practice—the moment an idea clarifies how to act.</p>
      <p>Rough at Sea is where I collect short entries, quotations, and small experiments: the useful fragments, the wrong turns, and the moments worth returning to.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about-details">
    <div class="shell about-grid">
      <p class="section-number">WORKING PRINCIPLES</p>
      <div class="belief-list">
        <article><span>01</span><h2>Capture the sentence.</h2><p>Keep the phrasing that made the idea stick; the exact words often matter more than a summary.</p></article>
        <article><span>02</span><h2>Let fragments meet.</h2><p>Group related notes by theme and let the connections reveal new meaning.</p></article>
        <article><span>03</span><h2>Write to return.</h2><p>Revisiting old notes is part of the practice—treat the book as living, not archival.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="now-section shell">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">NOW</p><h2>Gathering, sorting,<br />and returning to notes.</h2></div>
    <div class="now-list">
      <p><span>Reading</span> Passages and quotes that deserve a second look.</p>
      <p><span>Writing</span> Short entries that feel like bookmarks and leads.</p>
      <p><span>Collecting</span> Patterns from books, projects, and everyday practice.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
